{"name":"Mount Etna","hex":"#3d484c","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Mount Etna","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["Etna, a volcano in Sicily"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Mount_Etna"}],"entries":[{"title":"Mount Etna","blocks":[{"text":"Mount Etna, or simply Etna, is an active stratovolcano on the east coast of Sicily, Italy, in the Metropolitan City of Catania, between the cities of Messina and Catania. It is located above the convergent plate margin between the African Plate and the Eurasian Plate. It is one of the tallest active volcanoes in Europe, and the tallest peak in Italy south of the Alps with a current height of 3,403 m (11,165 ft), though this varies with summit eruptions. For instance, in 2021 the southeastern crater reached a height of 3,357 m (11,014 ft), but was then surpassed by the Voragine crater after the summer 2024 eruptions."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/39/Mt_Etna_and_Catania1.jpg/330px-Mt_Etna_and_Catania1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mount_Etna","wikidata":"Q16990"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0b/Mount_Etna_overview%2C_SRTMGL1.png/500px-Mount_Etna_overview%2C_SRTMGL1.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0b/Mount_Etna_overview%2C_SRTMGL1.png/1280px-Mount_Etna_overview%2C_SRTMGL1.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0b/Mount_Etna_overview%2C_SRTMGL1.png/500px-Mount_Etna_overview%2C_SRTMGL1.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Topographic map of Mount Etna and its surroundings","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMount_Etna_overview%2C_SRTMGL1.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/95/Etna_multidirectional_Hillshade.png/500px-Etna_multidirectional_Hillshade.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/95/Etna_multidirectional_Hillshade.png/1280px-Etna_multidirectional_Hillshade.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/95/Etna_multidirectional_Hillshade.png/500px-Etna_multidirectional_Hillshade.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Multidirectional hillshade relief of Mount Etna showing the summit and Valle del Bove on the lower right","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AEtna_multidirectional_Hillshade.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/aa/Mount_Etna_2021_eruption.jpg/500px-Mount_Etna_2021_eruption.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/aa/Mount_Etna_2021_eruption.jpg/1280px-Mount_Etna_2021_eruption.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/aa/Mount_Etna_2021_eruption.jpg/500px-Mount_Etna_2021_eruption.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"February 2021 eruption seen from Naval Air Station Sigonella","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMount_Etna_2021_eruption.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/51/Etna_storia_geologica.png/500px-Etna_storia_geologica.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/51/Etna_storia_geologica.png/500px-Etna_storia_geologica.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Simplified geological cross section of the Mount Etna volcanic complex (not to scale), showing its evolution from an early stage of submarine fissural activity, producing pillow lavas and a first shield volcano, to a subsequent mixed effusive and explosive activity building three main stratovolcano stages (Monte Calanna; Trifoglietto 1; Trifoglietto 2), then to the present Mongibello system (which has developed in two successive stages from about 15,000 years ago). The volcanic activity has gradually shifted from SE to NW (from offshore to onshore). The Valle del Bove is the former eastern flank of the volcano, which collapsed about 64,000 years ago and thus allows the older volcanic edifices to be recognized.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AEtna_storia_geologica.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5f/Mount_Etna_from_the_south_060313.JPG/500px-Mount_Etna_from_the_south_060313.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5f/Mount_Etna_from_the_south_060313.JPG/1280px-Mount_Etna_from_the_south_060313.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5f/Mount_Etna_from_the_south_060313.JPG/500px-Mount_Etna_from_the_south_060313.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Mount Etna from the south with the smoking peak in the upper left and a lateral crater in the centre","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMount_Etna_from_the_south_060313.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5d/Eruzione_dell%27Etna_del_1766%2C_incisione_colorata_di_Alessandro_D%27Anna.jpg/500px-Eruzione_dell%27Etna_del_1766%2C_incisione_colorata_di_Alessandro_D%27Anna.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5d/Eruzione_dell%27Etna_del_1766%2